  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 201 PM MDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nHot conditions remain in place today with low elevations in the\nmid to upper 90s with localized areas reaching 100. Heat\nadvisory for much of the area remains in effect until 11 pm.\nOnly very low chance of showers and thunderstorms in southern\nmountains. General dry conditions expected through mid week with\na cooling trend as upper ridge flattens a bit with more of a\nwesterly push. Areas of smoke will remain for the next couple of\ndays as well with Custer County still in an air quality\nadvisory. By late week flow aloft becomes more southwesterly\nwhich may allow some of the monsoonal moisture to return with a\nchance of showers and thunderstorms in the grids Thursday\nthrough next Saturday. Temperatures fall to below normal with\nthe expected cloud cover Thursday through Saturday as well with\nlow elevations in the upper 70s and 80s and mountains mainly\nupper 60s and 70s.",
